<!-- Welcome Section -->

## Welcome

This professional learning module is designed to help you prepare to teach Unit 2: Machine Learning Fundamentals from CodeAI's **Building AI Systems** curriculum, available at <a href="[INSERT COURSE LINK]" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Building AI Systems</a>.

Building AI Systems is a year-long course for high school students, built as part of a Career and Technical Education (CTE) pathway aligned to the Microsoft Azure AI-901 certification exam.

<!-- Goals Section -->
<div style="margin: 20px auto; width: 90%; max-width: 900px; background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); font-size: 14pt;">
    <h2>In this module, you will:</h2>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Explain machine learning as a shift from writing explicit rules to learning patterns from data, and how that differs from the logic-based AI taught in Unit 1.</li><br>
        <li>Read and reason through data literacy basics, categorical vs. numerical data, correlation, outliers, confidently enough to guide students through their first data-driven decisions.</li><br>
        <li>Build and evaluate both regression and classification models, understanding loss, accuracy, recall, and precision well enough to explain why one model beats another.</li><br>
        <li>Reason about bias, representativeness, and feature selection, recognizing how the data and choices behind a model shape what it can and can't do.</li><br>
        <li>Guide real conversations about fairness, safety, and accountability, and understand how this unit aligns to AI-901's Domain 1 content.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

**Suggested Total Time:** 155 minutes

**Lesson One Suggested Time:** 15 minutes

---

## Take the Pre-Survey

CodeAI values and is responsive to feedback. Please fill out the pre-survey to tell us about who you are and how we can best support you.

